{
 "The Scales": "天秤",
 "23 September – 22 October": "9月23日 – 10月22日",
 "Harmony": "和谐",
 "Fairness": "公正",
 "Diplomacy": "圆融",
 "Beauty": "美",
 "Partnership": "伙伴关系",
 "Grace under pressure": "压力下的优雅",
 "Libra people walk into a room and quietly take its temperature. Before they have said very much, they have noticed who feels left out, which two people are not speaking, and whether the lighting is doing anyone any favours. This is the sign of the Scales, ruled by Venus, and its whole life is an ongoing conversation about fairness, beauty and how people can live alongside one another without anyone being flattened.": "天秤座的人走进一个房间，会悄悄地测一测它的温度。在还没说几句话之前，他们已经注意到谁觉得被冷落了，哪两个人互不说话，以及灯光是不是让谁显得不太好看。这是天秤的星座，由金星守护，它的一生都是一场关于公正、美，以及人们如何能比邻而居、又不让任何人被压扁的持续对话。",
 "As a cardinal air sign, Libra starts things through relationship. Where other signs begin with force or ambition, Libra begins with an invitation: a dinner, an introduction, a gentle suggestion that perhaps there is another way to see this. Libra people tend to think best out loud and in company. An idea becomes real to them once it has been weighed against someone else's view, which is why they can seem undecided when in fact they are still gathering the other half of the picture.": "作为本位风象星座，天秤座通过关系来开启事情。别的星座以力量或野心起步，天秤座则以一份邀请起步：一顿晚餐、一次引荐、一个温和的提议——也许还有另一种看待这件事的方式。天秤座的人往往在说出来、在有人陪伴时思考得最好。一个想法要先和别人的观点放在一起掂量过，对他们来说才变得真实，所以他们看起来像是拿不定主意，其实他们只是还在收集画面的另一半。",
 "There is real steel under the charm. Libra cares deeply about justice, and when something is plainly unfair it can become surprisingly fierce on someone else's behalf. The polished manner is not decoration; it is a strategy for keeping the peace long enough for the truth to be heard.": "魅力之下有真正的钢筋。天秤座深深在乎公正，当某件事明显不公平时，它为别人出头的样子可能凶猛得出人意料。那份得体的举止并不是装饰，而是一种策略：让和平维持得足够久，好让真相被听见。",
 "The deeper work for Libra is learning that balance is not the same as stillness. Scales that never move are broken. A balanced life tips, corrects and tips again, and some of the most important moments are the ones where Libra chooses a side, says what it wants, and lets the room adjust. When Libra trusts its own taste and judgement as much as it trusts everyone else's, it becomes what it was always meant to be: a person who makes the world a little more graceful, and a little more just, simply by being in it.": "天秤座更深的功课，是学会平衡并不等于静止。一架从不摆动的天平是坏掉的。平衡的生活会倾斜、校正、再倾斜，而有些最重要的时刻，正是天秤座选择一边、说出自己想要什么、让整个房间去适应的时候。当天秤座信任自己的品味和判断，就像信任其他所有人的一样，它就成了它本来就该成为的样子：一个只要身在其中，就能让世界多一点优雅、多一点公正的人。",
 "Libra's great gift is the ability to see a situation from more than one side and to say so kindly. Libra people are natural mediators, the friend who can translate one person's hurt into language the other can actually hear. They have an eye for proportion — in a room, an outfit, a sentence or a plan — and they can make the ordinary feel considered and lovely. They are genuinely good company: curious about people, quick to laugh, generous with compliments that are specific rather than empty. Underneath the ease is a strong moral compass. Libra notices when a rule falls harder on some people than on others, and it will keep working, politely and persistently, until the arrangement is fairer.": "天秤座最大的天赋，是能从不止一面看一个处境，并且温和地说出来。天秤座的人是天生的调解者，是那个能把一个人的伤痛翻译成另一个人真正听得进去的语言的朋友。他们对比例很有眼光——无论是一个房间、一身装扮、一句话还是一个计划——能让平凡之物显得用心而可爱。他们是真正的好伙伴：对人好奇，爱笑，赞美慷慨而且具体，不是空话。在这份从容之下，是一个坚定的道德罗盘。天秤座会注意到一条规则对某些人比对另一些人更严苛，并且会礼貌而执着地一直努力，直到安排变得更公平。",
 "The shadow side of all that consideration is a habit of disappearing into other people's preferences. Libra people can say \"I don't mind\" so often that they lose track of what they do mind, and the resentment surfaces later, sideways, as coolness or a sudden exit. Decisions can stall because every option carries a cost to someone. Avoiding conflict can slide into telling each person what they want to hear, which feels kind in the moment and complicated afterwards. There can also be a quiet perfectionism about how things look from the outside. The growth edge is simple to describe and hard to practise: form an opinion before asking for one, and accept that a little friction is the price of an honest relationship.": "所有这些体贴的阴影面，是一种消失在别人偏好里的习惯。天秤座的人可能说了太多次“我无所谓”，以至于弄不清自己到底在意什么，而怨气会在之后以侧面的方式冒出来，变成冷淡或突然离场。决定可能会停滞，因为每个选项都会让某个人付出代价。回避冲突可能滑向对每个人说他们想听的话，这在当下感觉很善良，事后却变得复杂。也可能有一种对外在观感的悄悄的完美主义。成长课题说起来简单，做起来难：先形成自己的看法，再去问别人的；并且接受，一点点摩擦是诚实关系的代价。",
 "Love is Libra's home territory, and Libra people tend to treat a relationship as something to be designed with care, like a shared room both people actually want to spend time in. They court beautifully: the thoughtful message, the well-chosen restaurant, the way they remember what you said three weeks ago and quietly act on it. They want a partner who is also a friend and a conversational equal, someone with whom ideas, plans and small daily rituals can be traded back and forth.": "爱情是天秤座的主场，天秤座的人往往把一段关系当作需要用心设计的东西，就像一间两个人都真心愿意待在里面的共享房间。他们追求得很美：用心的消息，精心挑选的餐厅，还有他们记得你三周前说过的话、并悄悄付诸行动的方式。他们想要一个同时也是朋友、在谈话上旗鼓相当的伴侣，可以彼此来回交换想法、计划和日常的小仪式。",
 "The risk is that Libra keeps the peace at the expense of the truth, smoothing over disagreements until they harden into a silence that is difficult to break. Libra may also fall for someone's potential rather than the person standing in front of it. The healthiest Libra love lets both people be a little inconvenient. Saying \"actually, I'd prefer this\" is not a threat to harmony; it is what makes the harmony real.": "风险在于天秤座以真相为代价来维持和平，把分歧抹平，直到它们硬化成一种难以打破的沉默。天秤座也可能爱上一个人的潜力，而不是站在潜力前面的那个人。最健康的天秤式爱情，允许两个人都有一点“不方便”。说“其实，我更想这样”并不是对和谐的威胁，它正是让和谐变得真实的东西。",
 "At work, Libra people shine wherever relationships, judgement and taste meet. They are skilled at reading a client, softening a hard message without losing its substance, and spotting the detail that makes a product, space or proposal feel finished. Roles involving negotiation, design, curation, advocacy, mediation, hospitality or any kind of partnership tend to suit them, as do collaborative teams where they can bring different people together.": "在工作中，凡是关系、判断与品味交汇的地方，天秤座的人都会闪光。他们擅长读懂客户，在不失去实质的前提下软化一条难听的消息，并发现那个让一件产品、一个空间或一份提案显得完整的细节。涉及谈判、设计、策展、倡导、调解、款待或任何形式合作的角色往往适合他们，能把不同的人聚在一起的协作团队也是。",
 "Libra does less well in cultures of constant aggression, or where every decision is made in isolation. It can also take on too much, because refusing a request feels rude. The professional growth edge is owning decisions: gathering views, yes, and then making the call and standing by it. When Libra does this, colleagues often discover that it was a natural leader all along.": "在持续充满攻击性的文化里，或者每个决定都孤立做出的地方，天秤座表现得没那么好。它也可能揽下太多，因为拒绝一个请求让它觉得失礼。职业上的成长课题是为决定负责：听取意见，当然要；然后拍板，并且坚持下去。当天秤座这样做时，同事们常常会发现，它一直都是天生的领导者。",
 "Libra people are deeply affected by their surroundings, so self-care often begins with beauty and order: clearing one surface, opening a window, putting fresh flowers where the eye falls first. Time alone matters more than Libra admits, because only in solitude does it hear its own preferences clearly. A simple Friday ritual suits this sign: light a pink or pale blue candle, write down three things you want — not three things others want from you — and choose one to honour over the weekend. Music, galleries and slow, pleasant meals with good company refill the cup.": "天秤座的人深受周围环境影响，所以自我照顾往往从美和秩序开始：清空一块台面，打开一扇窗，把鲜花放在目光最先落下的地方。独处比天秤座承认的更重要，因为只有在独处中，它才能清楚地听见自己的偏好。一个简单的周五仪式很适合这个星座：点一支粉色或淡蓝色的蜡烛，写下三件你想要的事——不是别人想从你这里得到的三件事——然后选一件在周末去实现。音乐、画廊，以及和好友一起慢慢享用的愉快餐食，都能把杯子重新斟满。",
 "Libra tends to find easy rapport with the other air signs, Gemini and Aquarius, through shared curiosity and a love of conversation. With the fire signs — Aries, Leo and Sagittarius — there is often attraction and momentum; fire brings decisiveness and Libra brings perspective. Aries, the opposite sign, can feel like a mirror, showing Libra the directness it is learning. Earth signs offer stability and sensual pleasure, though pace and priorities may need talking through. Water signs bring emotional depth that can enrich Libra, provided feelings are named rather than politely sidestepped. As always, the whole birth chart matters far more than the Sun alone.": "天秤座往往通过共同的好奇心和对交谈的热爱，与另外两个风象星座双子座和水瓶座轻松融洽。和火象星座——白羊座、狮子座和射手座——之间常常有吸引力和推动力；火带来果断，天秤带来视角。对宫的白羊座可能像一面镜子，照出天秤座正在学习的直接。土象星座提供稳定和感官上的愉悦，不过节奏和优先次序可能需要好好谈一谈。水象星座带来能丰富天秤座的情感深度，前提是感受被说出来，而不是被礼貌地绕开。一如既往，整张星盘远比单看太阳重要。",
 "The Scorpion": "蝎子",
 "23 October – 21 November": "10月23日 – 11月21日",
 "Pluto (traditionally Mars)": "冥王星（传统上为火星）",
 "Depth": "深度",
 "Intensity": "强烈",
 "Loyalty": "忠诚",
 "Transformation": "蜕变",
 "Insight": "洞察",
 "Privacy": "隐私",
 "Scorpio people rarely tell you everything at once, and they notice a great deal more than they let on. Ask a Scorpio how they are and you may get a polite, closed answer; spend a long evening with one and you may find yourself telling them things you have never said aloud. This is the fixed water sign, ruled by Pluto (traditionally Mars), and its territory is everything beneath the surface: motive, desire, loyalty, power, and the feelings most people would rather not look at directly.": "天蝎座的人很少一下子把什么都告诉你，而他们注意到的远比表现出来的多。问天蝎座的人过得怎么样，你可能得到一个礼貌而封闭的回答；和天蝎座的人共度一个漫长的夜晚，你可能会发现自己说出了从未说出口的事。这是固定水象星座，由冥王星守护（传统上为火星），它的领地是表面之下的一切：动机、欲望、忠诚、权力，以及大多数人宁愿不去直视的感受。",
 "Water gives Scorpio its emotional depth; fixity gives that depth staying power. Scorpio feelings do not pass like weather. They settle in, they are remembered, and they shape what happens next. This is why Scorpio people are so committed when they love, so tenacious when they decide, and so slow to forgive a genuine betrayal. It is also why they are capable of extraordinary change. The Scorpio story is one of shedding skin: going through something hard, letting an old self end, and emerging with more truth than before.": "水给了天蝎座情感的深度；固定给了这份深度持久力。天蝎座的感受不像天气那样一过就散。它们会沉淀下来，会被记住，并塑造接下来发生的事。这就是为什么天蝎座的人爱的时候如此投入，下定决心时如此坚韧，面对真正的背叛又如此难以原谅。这也是为什么他们能够发生非凡的改变。天蝎座的故事是一个蜕皮的故事：经历一件艰难的事，让一个旧的自己结束，然后带着比以前更多的真实重新浮现。",
 "People sometimes mistake Scorpio's privacy for coldness, or its intensity for drama. In fact, Scorpio people are often calm in a crisis precisely because they have already imagined the worst and made their peace with it. They can sit with someone's grief, anger or shame without flinching, which makes them rare and valuable friends.": "人们有时会把天蝎座的隐私误认为冷漠，把它的强烈误认为戏剧化。事实上，天蝎座的人在危机中常常很冷静，正是因为他们早已想象过最坏的情况，并与之和解了。他们能陪着一个人的悲伤、愤怒或羞耻而不退缩，这让他们成为难得而珍贵的朋友。",
 "The growth edge for Scorpio is trust. The instinct to protect the soft centre is wise, but a life lived entirely behind armour becomes lonely. When Scorpio learns to let a few people see the process rather than only the result — the doubt, the longing, the tenderness — its power softens into something even stronger: depth that heals, rather than depth that guards.": "天蝎座的成长课题是信任。保护柔软内核的本能是明智的，但一种完全活在盔甲后面的生活会变得孤独。当天蝎座学会让少数几个人看到过程，而不只是结果——那份怀疑、渴望和温柔——它的力量就会软化成某种更强大的东西：疗愈的深度，而不是防守的深度。",
 "Scorpio brings a focus that most signs can only envy. When Scorpio people care about something, they go all the way down, researching, feeling and committing until they understand it properly. They are perceptive about motives and can usually tell when a smile and its meaning do not match. Their loyalty is fierce and practical; they are the friend who turns up, keeps secrets and remembers. Scorpio handles difficult subjects with unusual courage, from money conversations to grief to desire, and its steadiness gives others permission to be honest too. Above all, Scorpio has a talent for renewal. It can lose something, rebuild from the ground up, and come back wiser rather than bitter.": "天蝎座带来一种大多数星座只能羡慕的专注。当天蝎座的人在乎一件事时，他们会一直深入到底，研究、感受、投入，直到真正理解它。他们对动机很敏锐，通常能分辨出一个笑容和它的含义是否对得上。他们的忠诚强烈而务实；他们是那个会出现、会保守秘密、会记得的朋友。天蝎座以少有的勇气处理艰难的话题，从金钱谈话到悲伤再到欲望，它的沉稳也让别人有了诚实的许可。最重要的是，天蝎座有一种更新的天赋。它可以失去一些东西，从头重建，然后变得更有智慧而不是更苦涩地回来。",
 "The same depth that makes Scorpio wise can make it suspicious. Scorpio people may test others quietly, waiting to see whether trust is deserved, and those tests can feel unfair to someone who never knew they were being examined. Hurt can turn into silence, or into a long memory that keeps score. There can be a pull towards control — of information, of outcomes, of how vulnerable they allow themselves to appear. All-or-nothing thinking can make small disappointments feel enormous. The constructive work is to name a feeling while it is still small, to give people a real chance to repair, and to remember that letting go of a grudge is a release, not a defeat.": "让天蝎座有智慧的那份深度，也可能让它多疑。天蝎座的人可能会悄悄考验别人，等着看信任是否值得给出，而这些考验对一个从不知道自己正在被检验的人来说可能显得不公平。伤害可能变成沉默，或者变成一份记账式的长久记忆。可能有一种想要控制的拉力——控制信息、控制结果、控制自己允许显露出多少脆弱。非此即彼的思维会让小小的失望显得巨大。建设性的功课是在感受还小的时候就说出来，给别人一个真正修复的机会，并记住放下怨恨是一种释放，而不是失败。",
 "Scorpio does not do casual feelings well, even when it does casual dating. Scorpio people want to be known completely and to know their partner the same way, which means intimacy matters far more to them than polish. Emotional honesty is the real seduction: the late-night conversation in which both people finally stop performing. For many with this Sun, physical and emotional closeness are tightly woven together.": "天蝎座不擅长随便的感情，即使它在随便地约会。天蝎座的人想要被完全了解，也想同样地了解伴侣，这意味着亲密对他们来说远比体面重要。情感上的诚实才是真正的诱惑：那场深夜的谈话，两个人终于都不再表演。对许多太阳在天蝎的人来说，身体上和情感上的亲近紧紧交织在一起。",
 "Once committed, Scorpio is protective, devoted and remarkably steady through hard times. The shadow shows up as jealousy, mind-reading, or withdrawing to punish rather than to rest. Partners can feel they are being tested. The healthiest Scorpio love replaces surveillance with conversation: \"I felt uneasy when that happened\" rather than a silent investigation. A partner who can meet Scorpio's intensity without being frightened of it — and who keeps their word — will find a lover of rare depth and loyalty.": "一旦投入，天蝎座保护欲强、全心付出，在艰难时期也稳得出奇。阴影表现为嫉妒、揣测对方心思，或者为了惩罚而不是为了休息而退缩。伴侣可能会觉得自己在被考验。最健康的天蝎式爱情用对话取代监视：说“那件事发生时我觉得不安”，而不是进行一场无声的调查。一个能迎接天蝎座的强烈而不被吓到的伴侣——并且说话算话——会找到一位深度与忠诚都罕见的爱人。",
 "Scorpio people make excellent investigators, strategists and specialists: anyone whose work involves seeing what others miss. Research, psychology and counselling, finance, investigation, crisis response, editing, data and security work, and roles that handle sensitive or confidential matters can all suit them well. They work best with autonomy and depth rather than constant interruption, and they are at their sharpest when the stakes are real.": "天蝎座的人是出色的调查者、策略家和专家：任何工作需要看见别人遗漏之处的人。研究、心理学与咨询、金融、调查、危机应对、编辑、数据与安全工作，以及处理敏感或机密事务的角色，都很适合他们。他们在有自主权和深度、而不是不断被打断的环境中工作得最好，在利害真实存在时最为敏锐。",
 "Scorpio is often the quiet power in a team: not the loudest voice, but the one whose view everyone waits for. The difficulties tend to be politics and trust; Scorpio may hold information back or assume hidden agendas where there are none. The professional growth edge is to share more of its thinking earlier, and to choose carefully which battles are really worth winning.": "天蝎座常常是团队里安静的力量：不是最响亮的声音，而是那个大家都在等待其观点的人。困难往往在于人际政治和信任；天蝎座可能会保留信息，或者在根本没有隐藏议程的地方假设有。职业上的成长课题是更早地分享更多想法，并仔细挑选哪些仗真正值得去赢。",
 "Scorpio people recharge in privacy and depth, not in crowds. A long bath, a walk beside dark water, an evening with the phone switched off, or a journal that nobody else will ever read can restore them quickly. Because Scorpio holds feelings so tightly, release matters: writing out anger and then tearing up the page, or simply crying without apology, can feel like setting down a heavy bag. The dark of the moon, just before the new moon, is a natural time for this sign to reflect on what it is finally ready to let go.": "天蝎座的人在隐私和深度中恢复能量，而不是在人群中。泡一个长长的澡，在幽暗的水边散步，关掉手机度过一个晚上，或者写一本永远不会有别人读的日记，都能很快让他们恢复。因为天蝎座把感受握得那么紧，释放就很重要：把愤怒写下来然后撕掉那页纸，或者干脆毫无歉意地哭一场，都会像放下一个沉重的包。月亮的暗期，就在新月之前，是这个星座反思自己终于准备好放下什么的自然时机。",
 "Scorpio often feels at home with the other water signs, Cancer and Pisces, who understand emotion without needing it explained. Earth signs — Taurus, Virgo and Capricorn — offer the steadiness and loyalty Scorpio values, and Taurus, the opposite sign, can be both a strong attraction and a lesson in simple pleasure and letting things be. Fire signs bring heat and boldness; the connection can be electric, though both may need to soften the urge to win. Air signs can feel too light at first, yet they help Scorpio talk feelings through rather than brood on them. The full chart tells the real story.": "天蝎座常常和另外两个水象星座巨蟹座和双鱼座在一起时感到自在，它们不需要解释就懂得情绪。土象星座——金牛座、处女座和摩羯座——提供天蝎座看重的稳定和忠诚，而对宫的金牛座既可能是一股强烈的吸引，也可能是一堂关于简单愉悦和顺其自然的课。火象星座带来热度和大胆；这种连接可能像通了电一样，不过双方都可能需要软化想赢的冲动。风象星座起初可能显得太轻，但它们能帮助天蝎座把感受说出来，而不是闷着反复咀嚼。完整的星盘才讲述真正的故事。",
 "The Archer": "射手",
 "22 November – 21 December": "11月22日 – 12月21日",
 "Adventure": "冒险",
 "Optimism": "乐观",
 "Honesty": "诚实",
 "Freedom": "自由",
 "Meaning": "意义",
 "Sagittarius people live with one eye on the horizon. They want to know what is over the next hill, behind the next idea, beneath the surface of an unfamiliar culture or philosophy, and they are happiest when life feels like a journey rather than a holding pattern. This is the Archer, a mutable fire sign ruled by Jupiter, and its arrow is always aimed at something further than where it currently stands.": "射手座的人活着时总有一只眼睛望着地平线。他们想知道下一座山丘那边有什么，下一个想法背后有什么，一种陌生文化或哲学的表面之下有什么，而当生活感觉像一段旅程而不是原地盘旋时，他们最快乐。这是射手，一个由木星守护的变动火象星座，它的箭总是瞄准比它此刻所在之处更远的地方。",
 "Fire gives Sagittarius warmth, enthusiasm and courage; mutability gives it restlessness and a talent for adapting. Together they create someone who can arrive in a strange town, find the best café by lunchtime and be swapping stories with strangers by evening. Yet the journeys are not only literal. Just as often they happen in the mind: reading three books at once, falling for a new way of seeing the world, signing up for a course on a whim, or asking the big questions over a late drink — what is the point of all this, and how should we live?": "火给了射手座温暖、热情和勇气；变动给了它不安分和适应的天赋。两者合在一起，造就了一个能到达陌生小镇、午饭前就找到最好的咖啡馆、傍晚已经在和陌生人交换故事的人。然而旅程不只是字面上的。同样经常地，它们发生在头脑里：同时读三本书，爱上一种看世界的新方式，一时兴起报名一门课，或者在深夜小酌时问出那些大问题——这一切的意义是什么，我们该怎样生活？",
 "Honesty is central to this sign. Sagittarius people tend to say what they see, often with humour and sometimes without much padding. They would rather be truthful and occasionally clumsy than polished and evasive. Their optimism is not naivety; it is a decision to believe that growth is possible, renewed each morning.": "诚实是这个星座的核心。射手座的人往往看到什么就说什么，常常带着幽默，有时也不怎么加缓冲。他们宁愿真诚而偶尔笨拙，也不愿圆滑而闪躲。他们的乐观不是天真，而是一个每天早晨重新做出的决定：相信成长是可能的。",
 "The growth edge for Sagittarius is depth and follow-through. Freedom is precious, but so is staying long enough for something to take root. When Sagittarius discovers that commitment can be another kind of adventure — that you can explore a single relationship, place or craft for years and still find new country in it — its wisdom stops being borrowed from the road and becomes genuinely its own.": "射手座的成长课题是深度和坚持到底。自由很珍贵，但留得足够久、让某样东西扎根也同样珍贵。当射手座发现承诺也可以是另一种冒险——你可以用许多年去探索一段关系、一个地方或一门手艺，依然在其中找到新的天地——它的智慧就不再是从路上借来的，而真正成为它自己的。",
 "Sagittarius people bring generosity of spirit wherever they go. They are funny, frank and quick to encourage, the friend who believes in your idea before you quite do. Their optimism is contagious, and they have a gift for finding the larger meaning in a setback, turning a disappointment into a story about what was learned. They are open-minded about people and cultures, curious about beliefs unlike their own, and often wonderful teachers because they love sharing whatever excites them. Sagittarius tends to be brave about change; when life shifts, it packs a bag, figuratively or literally, and goes out to meet it. That willingness to say yes opens doors for everyone around them.": "射手座的人无论走到哪里都带着精神上的慷慨。他们风趣、坦率、乐于鼓励，是那个在你自己还没完全相信之前就相信你的点子的朋友。他们的乐观很有感染力，他们有一种在挫折中找到更大意义的天赋，把一次失望变成一个关于学到了什么的故事。他们对人和文化持开放态度，对与自己不同的信仰充满好奇，而且常常是出色的老师，因为他们热爱分享任何让自己兴奋的东西。射手座往往勇于面对改变；当生活发生转变时，它会收拾行囊——比喻意义上或字面意义上——出门去迎接它。那份愿意说“好”的心意，为身边的每个人打开了门。",
 "The Archer's shadow is the arrow fired before looking. Sagittarius people can promise more than they can deliver, agree to plans in a burst of enthusiasm and quietly slip away when the routine part begins. Their honesty sometimes lands as tactlessness, and they can be genuinely surprised when a joke hurts. Restlessness may pull them out of situations just as those situations become meaningful, and a strongly held belief can harden into preaching. Boredom is a real enemy, and novelty can become a way of outrunning an uncomfortable feeling. The constructive work is to finish one thing before beginning the next, to ask before advising, and to notice when freedom has quietly become a way of avoiding closeness.": "射手的阴影是还没看清就射出的箭。射手座的人可能承诺得比能做到的多，在一阵热情中答应计划，然后在例行部分开始时悄悄溜走。他们的诚实有时会显得不够得体，当一个玩笑伤了人时，他们可能真心感到意外。不安分可能恰好在某些处境开始变得有意义时把他们拉出来，而一个坚定的信念也可能硬化成说教。无聊是真正的敌人，新鲜感可能成为逃离不舒服感受的一种方式。建设性的功课是做完一件事再开始下一件，先询问再给建议，并留意自由何时已悄悄变成回避亲近的一种方式。",
 "Sagittarius falls in love with a person and with the life the two of them might explore together. Early romance often feels like an expedition: spontaneous trips, long talks about everything, a shared sense of humour that makes ordinary days feel bright. Sagittarius people need a partner who is also a companion and a fellow student of life, someone with their own passions who does not require constant reassurance.": "射手座爱上的，是一个人，以及两个人可能一起探索的生活。最初的浪漫常常像一次远征：说走就走的旅行，无所不谈的长谈，一种让平凡日子都显得明亮的共同幽默感。射手座的人需要一个同时也是同伴、是一起学习人生的同学的伴侣，一个有自己的热情、不需要持续安慰的人。",
 "Space is not a lack of love for this sign. Sagittarius shows devotion by including you in its plans, telling you the truth and wanting you to grow as well. Trouble comes when emotional needs start to feel like restrictions, or when bluntness bruises a more sensitive partner. Lasting Sagittarius love is built on trust and honest freedom: clear agreements, regular new experiences together, and a willingness to stay present through the dull or difficult chapters, which turn out to be part of the journey too.": "对这个星座来说，空间并不意味着缺少爱。射手座表达忠诚的方式，是把你纳入它的计划，对你说真话，也希望你同样成长。麻烦出现在情感需求开始感觉像束缚的时候，或者当直率伤到了一个更敏感的伴侣的时候。持久的射手式爱情建立在信任和诚实的自由之上：清楚的约定，定期一起拥有新的经历，以及愿意在乏味或艰难的篇章里依然在场——事实证明，那些篇章也是旅程的一部分。",
 "Sagittarius people thrive in work that has meaning, movement and room to grow. Teaching, publishing, travel and tourism, outdoor work, law, coaching, broadcasting, international roles, selling something they genuinely believe in, and anything built around big ideas can all suit them. They are inspiring pitchers and natural motivators, at their best when the vision is clear and the rules are not too tight.": "射手座的人在有意义、有流动、有成长空间的工作中如鱼得水。教学、出版、旅行与旅游、户外工作、法律、教练、广播、国际性的角色、推销他们真心相信的东西，以及任何围绕宏大理念建立的事业，都很适合他们。他们是鼓舞人心的提案者和天生的激励者，在愿景清晰、规则不太紧的时候处于最佳状态。",
 "Repetitive tasks and heavy micromanagement drain them quickly. The professional shadow is overcommitment and patchy follow-through: brilliant openings, vague middles. Sagittarius benefits from colleagues or systems that handle detail, and from breaking big goals into small, visible steps it can tick off. When the Archer learns to aim for one specific target rather than the whole sky, its results become as impressive as its enthusiasm.": "重复性的任务和严密的微观管理很快就会让他们耗尽。职业上的阴影是过度承诺和断断续续的执行：开头精彩，中段模糊。射手座会从处理细节的同事或系统中受益，也会从把大目标拆成可以一个个打勾的小而可见的步骤中受益。当射手学会瞄准一个具体的靶子，而不是整片天空，它的成果就会和它的热情一样令人惊叹。",
 "Sagittarius people recharge through movement, open space and something new to think about. A long walk without a destination, a day trip to a town they have never visited, or an afternoon in a library chasing a fresh subject can reset their mood completely. Because they say yes to so much, they also need unscheduled time with no plans at all. A simple waxing moon ritual suits this sign: write a single intention on a strip of paper, fold it into the shape of an arrow and keep it somewhere visible, as a reminder of where you are aiming.": "射手座的人通过活动、开阔的空间和一些可以思考的新东西来恢复能量。一次没有目的地的长距离散步，去一个从未去过的小镇的一日游，或者在图书馆里追逐一个新课题的一个下午，都能彻底重置他们的心情。因为他们对那么多事情说“好”，他们也需要完全没有安排、没有计划的时间。一个简单的盈月仪式很适合这个星座：在一张纸条上写下一个意图，把它折成箭的形状，放在看得见的地方，提醒你自己正在瞄准哪里。",
 "Sagittarius often clicks quickly with the other fire signs, Aries and Leo, through shared enthusiasm, courage and a taste for fun. Air signs — Gemini, Libra and Aquarius — feed its curiosity and keep conversations lively; Gemini, the opposite sign, can feel like a brilliant sparring partner who teaches Sagittarius to value detail and listening. Earth signs offer grounding and help turn big plans into something real, though they may want more routine than Sagittarius enjoys. Water signs bring emotional depth and tenderness, which can open Sagittarius up if both respect each other's pace. The whole chart always matters more than the Sun.": "射手座常常和另外两个火象星座白羊座和狮子座一拍即合，靠的是共同的热情、勇气和对乐趣的喜爱。风象星座——双子座、天秤座和水瓶座——滋养它的好奇心，让谈话保持活跃；对宫的双子座可能像一位出色的切磋对手，教射手座重视细节和倾听。土象星座提供落地感，帮助把宏大的计划变成真实的东西，不过它们可能想要比射手座喜欢的更多的规律。水象星座带来情感深度和温柔，只要双方尊重彼此的节奏，就能让射手座敞开。整张星盘永远比太阳更重要。",
 "The Sea-Goat": "海山羊",
 "22 December – 19 January": "12月22日 – 1月19日",
 "Ambition": "抱负",
 "Discipline": "自律",
 "Responsibility": "责任",
 "Integrity": "正直",
 "Dry humour": "冷幽默",
 "Capricorn people often seem to have been born old and to grow younger as the years go by. Responsibility tends to arrive early for them, whether by circumstance or by temperament, and they learn quickly that wishing does not build anything — effort, patience and good judgement do. This is the Sea-Goat, a cardinal earth sign ruled by Saturn, and its symbol says a great deal: a creature able to climb the steepest mountain, with the tail of something that once came from the deep.": "摩羯座的人常常像是生来就老成，然后随着岁月流逝越活越年轻。责任往往很早就降临到他们身上，无论是出于境遇还是出于性情，他们很快就明白，光靠希望什么也建不起来——努力、耐心和良好的判断才能。这是海山羊，一个由土星守护的本位土象星座，它的符号说明了很多：一种能攀登最陡峭山峰的生灵，却长着一条来自深海的尾巴。",
 "As a cardinal sign, Capricorn initiates. As an earth sign, it initiates in practical ways: building a career, a home, a business, a reputation or a structure that other people can rely on. Capricorn people think in years rather than weeks. They understand that small, consistent actions compound, and they are willing to do the unglamorous work while others are still talking about their plans.": "作为本位星座，摩羯座开启事情。作为土象星座，它以务实的方式开启：建立一份事业、一个家、一门生意、一种声誉，或者一个别人可以依靠的结构。摩羯座的人以年而不是以周来思考。他们明白，小而持续的行动会累积复利，在别人还在谈论自己的计划时，他们愿意去做那些不光鲜的工作。",
 "There is far more warmth here than the reputation suggests. Capricorn's humour is dry, quick and often wonderfully dark, and its care is shown through action: fixing the problem, making the call, quietly paying attention to what you need. Many Capricorn people carry a hidden sensitivity, the Sea-Goat's tail, which they protect with competence and reserve.": "这里的温暖远比名声所暗示的多。摩羯座的幽默干巴巴的、来得快，常常带着绝妙的黑色意味，而它的关心通过行动来表达：解决问题，打那通电话，悄悄留意你需要什么。许多摩羯座的人带着一份隐藏的敏感，也就是海山羊的那条尾巴，他们用能干和矜持来保护它。",
 "The growth edge for Capricorn is rest and self-worth. Achievement is satisfying, but it cannot carry the whole weight of feeling worthwhile. When Capricorn learns that it is valuable before it accomplishes anything, that play is not wasted time and that it may lean on others too, its natural authority becomes gentler and far more sustainable. The mountain is still there to climb — but the view from each ledge can finally be enjoyed.": "摩羯座的成长课题是休息和自我价值。成就令人满足，但它无法承担“觉得自己有价值”的全部重量。当摩羯座学会在成就任何事之前自己就已经有价值，玩乐并不是浪费时间，自己也可以依靠别人，它天生的权威就会变得更温和，也更可持续得多。山依然在那里等着攀登——但从每一处岩架望出去的风景，终于可以被享受了。",
 "Capricorn's great strength is a reliability that goes all the way through. When Capricorn people commit, they deliver, and they do so without needing applause. They are realistic planners who can see every step between here and the goal, and they keep going long after motivation fades. Their judgement is usually sound because it rests on experience rather than wishful thinking. They respect tradition without being trapped by it, and they are skilled at building structures — teams, routines, savings habits, family rituals — that support other people long after the work is done. Add a sharp, understated sense of humour and a deep loyalty to those they love, and you have a quietly formidable ally.": "摩羯座最大的力量，是一种从里到外的可靠。摩羯座的人一旦承诺就会兑现，而且不需要掌声。他们是现实的规划者，能看清从这里到目标之间的每一步，在动力褪去很久之后依然坚持下去。他们的判断通常很可靠，因为它建立在经验而不是一厢情愿之上。他们尊重传统而不被传统困住，擅长建立结构——团队、日常规律、储蓄习惯、家庭仪式——在工作完成很久之后依然支撑着别人。再加上一种敏锐而含蓄的幽默感，以及对所爱之人深深的忠诚，你就拥有了一位安静却令人敬畏的盟友。",
 "The Sea-Goat's shadow is a climb that never stops. Capricorn people can tie their worth to productivity so tightly that rest feels like failure, and they may postpone joy until some future milestone that keeps moving further away. Pessimism can pass itself off as realism, and a fear of looking foolish can stop them trying anything new. They sometimes take on everyone's responsibilities and then resent being relied upon. Emotional reserve can read as coldness to people who do not yet know them well. The constructive path is to schedule pleasure as seriously as work, to share worries before they become burdens, and to accept that being human is not the same as being inefficient.": "海山羊的阴影是一场永不停止的攀登。摩羯座的人可能把自己的价值和生产力绑得太紧，以至于休息感觉像失败，他们可能把快乐推迟到某个未来的里程碑，而那个里程碑却越移越远。悲观可能伪装成现实，害怕显得愚蠢可能让他们不敢尝试任何新事物。他们有时会揽下所有人的责任，然后又怨恨自己被依赖。情感上的矜持在还不熟悉他们的人看来可能像冷漠。建设性的道路是像安排工作一样认真地安排乐趣，在担忧变成负担之前就说出来，并接受“身为人”并不等于“低效”。",
 "Capricorn approaches love carefully, because it intends to keep what it chooses. Capricorn people may take their time before opening up, watching whether a potential partner is consistent, kind and true to their word. Once they are in, they show love through steadiness: remembering the practical details, making plans for a shared future, turning up when it matters and staying through difficult seasons.": "摩羯座对待爱情很谨慎，因为它打算留住自己选择的东西。摩羯座的人在敞开心扉之前可能会花些时间，观察一位潜在伴侣是否始终如一、是否善良、是否说话算话。一旦投入，他们通过稳定来表达爱：记住实际的细节，为共同的未来做计划，在重要的时候出现，并在艰难的季节里留下来。",
 "Romance with Capricorn usually deepens with time. The reserve softens, the dry humour comes out, and a surprisingly sensual, affectionate side appears. The difficulty is that work or duty can crowd out intimacy, and feelings may be expressed through doing rather than saying, leaving a partner unsure where they stand. Capricorn grows in love by naming its feelings aloud, making room for spontaneity, and letting a partner support it rather than always being the one who holds everything together.": "和摩羯座的浪漫通常会随着时间加深。矜持变得柔软，冷幽默跑了出来，一个出人意料地感性、深情的一面显现出来。困难在于工作或责任可能挤掉亲密，感受可能通过做而不是说来表达，让伴侣不确定自己处在什么位置。摩羯座在爱情中的成长，是把感受大声说出来，为即兴留出空间，并让伴侣支持它，而不是永远做那个把一切撑在一起的人。",
 "Work matters deeply to Capricorn, not only as income but as a way of building something worthwhile. Capricorn people tend to do well in management, administration, finance, law, architecture, engineering, public service, skilled trades and any field that rewards patience and expertise. They are often the steady hand who, over time, quietly becomes the person everyone consults.": "工作对摩羯座意义重大，不只是作为收入，更是作为建立有价值之物的一种方式。摩羯座的人往往在管理、行政、金融、法律、建筑、工程、公共服务、技术行业，以及任何奖励耐心和专业的领域表现出色。他们常常是那只稳定的手，随着时间推移，悄悄成为每个人都会来请教的那个人。",
 "They respect clear structures and earned authority, and they can be frustrated by chaos, vagueness or people who want results without effort. The shadow is overwork and a reluctance to delegate, alongside a habit of measuring themselves only by status or output. Capricorn thrives professionally when it sets boundaries around its time, celebrates progress along the way and remembers that its long view is a gift to others, not just a burden it carries alone.": "他们尊重清晰的结构和靠实力赢得的权威，可能会对混乱、含糊或不想付出努力就要结果的人感到沮丧。阴影是过度工作和不愿授权，再加上只用地位或产出来衡量自己的习惯。当摩羯座为自己的时间设立边界，一路庆祝进展，并记住它的长远眼光是给别人的礼物，而不只是它独自背负的重担时，它在职业上就会茁壮成长。",
 "Capricorn people often need permission to stop, so self-care works best when it is written into the calendar like any other commitment. Time in nature, especially among hills, old trees or weathered stone, has a grounding effect on this sign. Simple, tactile activities — cooking a slow meal, gardening, working with clay or wood — let the mind rest while the hands stay busy. A Saturday ritual can help: hold a smooth stone, name one thing you achieved this week, and one thing you will let yourself enjoy without having to earn it.": "摩羯座的人常常需要被允许停下来，所以把自我照顾像其他承诺一样写进日程时效果最好。待在大自然里，尤其是在山丘、古树或风化的岩石之间，对这个星座有落地的作用。简单、有触感的活动——慢慢做一顿饭、园艺、玩黏土或木头——让头脑休息而双手保持忙碌。一个周六仪式会有帮助：握住一块光滑的石头，说出你这周完成的一件事，以及一件你允许自己不必挣来就可以享受的事。",
 "Capricorn tends to feel understood by the other earth signs, Taurus and Virgo, who share its practical outlook and respect for effort. Water signs — Cancer, Scorpio and Pisces — can soften Capricorn and draw out its tender side; Cancer, the opposite sign, often feels like a lesson in emotional nourishment and the meaning of home. Fire signs bring spark and ambition, though they may find Capricorn cautious while Capricorn finds them impulsive. Air signs offer new perspectives and a lighter touch, which can be refreshing if both value each other's different pace. The full birth chart reveals far more than the Sun.": "摩羯座往往觉得被另外两个土象星座金牛座和处女座理解，它们共享它务实的眼光和对努力的尊重。水象星座——巨蟹座、天蝎座和双鱼座——能软化摩羯座，引出它温柔的一面；对宫的巨蟹座常常像一堂关于情感滋养和家的意义的课。火象星座带来火花和抱负，不过它们可能觉得摩羯座太谨慎，而摩羯座觉得它们太冲动。风象星座提供新的视角和更轻盈的触感，只要双方珍视彼此不同的节奏，就会让人耳目一新。完整的星盘揭示的远比太阳多。",
 "The Water Bearer": "持水者",
 "20 January – 18 February": "1月20日 – 2月18日",
 "Uranus (traditionally Saturn)": "天王星（传统上为土星）",
 "Originality": "独创",
 "Independence": "独立",
 "Community": "社群",
 "Vision": "远见",
 "Friendship": "友谊",
 "Principle": "原则",
 "Aquarius people tend to look at the world as though they have just arrived from somewhere slightly more interesting. They notice the assumption nobody else questions, the rule that exists only because it always has, and the person on the edge of the group who has something worth saying. This is the Water Bearer, a fixed air sign ruled by Uranus (traditionally Saturn), and despite its name it is not a water sign: what it pours out is ideas, perspective and a sense of what the future could be.": "水瓶座的人看世界的样子，往往像是刚从某个更有意思一点的地方来到这里。他们注意到没有人质疑的那个假设，那条只因“一直如此”而存在的规则，以及群体边缘那个有话值得一说的人。这是持水者，一个由天王星守护（传统上为土星）的固定风象星座，尽管名字里有“水”，它并不是水象星座：它倾倒出来的是想法、视角，以及对未来可能是什么样子的感知。",
 "The double rulership explains much of the Aquarius character. Uranus brings originality, sudden insight and a love of freedom. Saturn brings structure, principle and a quiet stubbornness. Together they create someone who is both unconventional and remarkably consistent — the person who will happily break with tradition, yet holds fast to their own values for decades.": "双重守护星解释了水瓶座性格的许多方面。天王星带来独创、突然的洞见和对自由的热爱。土星带来结构、原则和一种安静的固执。两者合在一起，造就了一个既不循常规又非常始终如一的人——那个乐于打破传统，却几十年如一日坚守自己价值观的人。",
 "Aquarius is the sign of friendship, community and the collective. Aquarius people often care deeply about people as a whole, about fairness, progress and belonging, and they can be wonderful friends: loyal, accepting of difference, and uninterested in judging anyone for being unusual. Yet they can find one-to-one emotional intensity uncomfortable, preferring to think about a feeling rather than sink into it.": "水瓶座是友谊、社群和集体的星座。水瓶座的人常常深切关心作为整体的人们，关心公平、进步和归属感，他们可以是很棒的朋友：忠诚，接纳差异，对评判任何人的与众不同毫无兴趣。然而他们可能会觉得一对一的情感强度令人不自在，宁愿去思考一种感受，而不是沉浸其中。",
 "The growth edge for Aquarius is closeness. It is easy for this sign to love humanity and still keep individual people at arm's length, or to treat detachment as a virtue when it is sometimes a defence. When Aquarius allows itself to need others — to be held, not just to help — its vision becomes warmer and more human. Then its ideas stop being merely clever and become genuinely kind, shaping communities in which everyone, Aquarius included, can belong.": "水瓶座的成长课题是亲近。这个星座很容易爱着全人类，却仍然与具体的个人保持一臂之遥，或者把疏离当作美德，而它有时其实是一种防御。当水瓶座允许自己需要别人——被拥抱，而不只是去帮助——它的愿景就会变得更温暖、更有人味。那时，它的想法就不再只是聪明，而是真正善良，塑造出每个人——包括水瓶座自己——都能归属的社群。",
 "Aquarius people bring originality and independence to everything they touch. They think for themselves, often see solutions others overlook, and are not easily swayed by fashion or pressure. Their friendship is a gift: open-minded, loyal and free of possessiveness, they make room for people to be exactly who they are. They tend to care about fairness on a large scale and will put real effort into causes, communities and projects that help others. Calm under pressure, they can step back from emotional chaos and offer a clear, objective view. Their humour is often quirky and unexpected, and their curiosity about technology, science, art or society keeps them young in spirit and endlessly interesting company.": "水瓶座的人为他们接触的一切带来独创和独立。他们独立思考，常常看到别人忽略的解决办法，也不容易被潮流或压力左右。他们的友谊是一份礼物：思想开放、忠诚、没有占有欲，他们为人们留出空间，让人们完全做自己。他们往往在宏观层面上关心公平，会为能帮助别人的事业、社群和项目付出真正的努力。他们在压力下保持冷静，能从情绪的混乱中退后一步，提供清晰而客观的看法。他们的幽默常常古怪而出人意料，他们对科技、科学、艺术或社会的好奇心，让他们精神上保持年轻，也永远是有趣的伙伴。",
 "The Water Bearer's shadow is distance. Aquarius people can retreat into their heads when feelings get messy, analysing an emotional moment instead of being present in it, which can leave loved ones feeling unseen. Independence can turn into a refusal to compromise, and fixity means a strong opinion may be very hard to shift, however open-minded they believe themselves to be. Sometimes they rebel simply because a rule exists, or hold themselves apart to avoid being ordinary. They may also give generously to a cause while neglecting their closest relationships. Growth comes from staying in the room during difficult emotions, and from accepting that needing people is not a weakness but a part of being human.": "持水者的阴影是距离。当感受变得一团糟时，水瓶座的人可能会退回自己的头脑里，分析一个情感时刻而不是置身其中，这会让所爱的人觉得没有被看见。独立可能变成拒绝妥协，而固定性意味着一个强烈的观点可能很难动摇，无论他们自认为多么开明。有时他们反叛只是因为有一条规则存在，或者为了避免平凡而刻意与人保持距离。他们也可能慷慨地为一项事业付出，却忽略了最亲近的关系。成长来自在艰难情绪中留在房间里，并接受需要别人不是软弱，而是身为人的一部分。",
 "For Aquarius, love usually starts as friendship and stays strongest when it keeps that quality. Aquarius people are drawn to minds first: someone unusual, curious and secure enough not to need constant reassurance. They value a partner who has their own life, opinions and friends, and they offer the same freedom in return. Unconventional arrangements, shared projects and long conversations about the future can all be part of the romance.": "对水瓶座来说，爱情通常从友谊开始，并在保持这种特质时最为牢固。水瓶座的人首先被头脑吸引：一个与众不同、好奇、足够有安全感而不需要持续安慰的人。他们看重一个有自己的生活、观点和朋友的伴侣，也会回馈同样的自由。不循常规的安排、共同的项目，以及关于未来的长谈，都可以是浪漫的一部分。",
 "The challenge is emotional availability. Aquarius may show care through ideas and practical help while struggling to express tenderness directly, and it can withdraw when a partner's feelings seem too intense. Partners may need to ask openly for warmth. Aquarius grows in love by recognising that closeness does not erase individuality. Letting someone truly know its inner world, quirks and fears included, may be the most radical thing Aquarius ever does in a relationship.": "挑战在于情感上的可及。水瓶座可能通过想法和实际帮助来表达关心，却难以直接表达温柔，当伴侣的感受显得太强烈时，它可能会退缩。伴侣可能需要坦率地要求温暖。水瓶座在爱情中的成长，是认识到亲近并不会抹去个性。让一个人真正了解它的内心世界，包括那些怪癖和恐惧，可能是水瓶座在一段关系中做过的最激进的事。",
 "Aquarius people do their best work when they can innovate, improve systems or serve a wider purpose. Technology, science, research, social enterprise, campaigning, community organising, design, broadcasting, astrology and anything future-focused can suit them. They are strong at seeing how things could work better and at connecting people around a shared vision.": "当水瓶座的人能够创新、改进系统或服务于更广泛的目标时，他们会做出最好的工作。科技、科学、研究、社会企业、倡议运动、社区组织、设计、广播、占星，以及任何面向未来的事情，都很适合他们。他们擅长看出事情如何能运作得更好，也擅长把人们团结在共同的愿景周围。",
 "They struggle with rigid hierarchies, office politics and rules that make no sense to them, and they may challenge authority head-on. The professional shadow is impatience with slower thinkers and a tendency to drift away from the detailed follow-through needed to make an idea real. Aquarius thrives with freedom, a mission it believes in and collaborators who enjoy practical structure. When it learns to persuade rather than simply disrupt, its influence becomes remarkable.": "他们难以适应僵化的等级制度、办公室政治，以及在他们看来毫无道理的规则，并且可能正面挑战权威。职业上的阴影是对思考较慢的人缺乏耐心，以及容易偏离那些把想法变成现实所需的细致执行。水瓶座在拥有自由、一个它相信的使命，以及喜欢务实结构的合作者时会茁壮成长。当它学会说服而不只是颠覆，它的影响力就会变得非凡。",
 "Aquarius people recharge by stepping away from other people's expectations and following their own curiosity. A solitary evening with a documentary, a stargazing walk, or time spent on an odd personal project can restore them. Because they live so much in the mind, gentle practices that bring them back into the body — stretching, dancing alone in the kitchen, a slow walk with no phone — are especially welcome. On the full moon, try writing a short letter to your future self about the life you are building, then reread last year's letter to see how far you have come.": "水瓶座的人通过远离别人的期待、追随自己的好奇心来恢复能量。一个人看纪录片的夜晚，一次观星散步，或者花时间在一个古怪的个人项目上，都能让他们恢复。因为他们那么多时间活在头脑里，能把他们带回身体的温和练习——伸展、独自在厨房里跳舞、不带手机慢慢散步——尤其受欢迎。在满月时，试着给未来的自己写一封短信，谈谈你正在建造的生活，然后重读去年的信，看看你已经走了多远。",
 "Aquarius often finds easy understanding with the other air signs, Gemini and Libra, through shared ideas and a love of conversation. Fire signs — Aries, Leo and Sagittarius — bring enthusiasm and boldness that can energise Aquarius; Leo, the opposite sign, frequently feels like a meeting of head and heart, teaching Aquarius about warmth and personal expression. Earth signs can give Aquarian visions a solid foundation, though differences in pace and tradition may need discussing. Water signs offer an emotional depth that can feel unfamiliar at first, yet it can help Aquarius open up. The whole chart matters most.": "水瓶座常常通过共同的想法和对交谈的热爱，与另外两个风象星座双子座和天秤座轻松相知。火象星座——白羊座、狮子座和射手座——带来能为水瓶座充电的热情和大胆；对宫的狮子座常常像是头脑与心灵的相遇，教会水瓶座温暖和个人表达。土象星座能给水瓶座的愿景一个坚实的基础，不过节奏和传统上的差异可能需要讨论。水象星座提供一种起初可能感觉陌生的情感深度，但它能帮助水瓶座敞开。整张星盘最重要。",
 "The Fish": "双鱼",
 "19 February – 20 March": "2月19日 – 3月20日",
 "Neptune (traditionally Jupiter)": "海王星（传统上为木星）",
 "Compassion": "慈悲",
 "Imagination": "想象力",
 "Intuition": "直觉",
 "Empathy": "共情",
 "Pisces people seem to live with a door left slightly open between this world and another. They pick up the mood of a room before anyone speaks, feel music with their whole being, and sometimes know what a friend needs before the friend does. This is the sign of the Fish, two of them swimming in opposite directions, a mutable water sign ruled by Neptune (traditionally Jupiter), and its nature is fluid, imaginative and deeply compassionate.": "双鱼座的人似乎活在一扇在这个世界和另一个世界之间微微敞开的门旁。他们在任何人开口之前就捕捉到房间的情绪，用整个生命去感受音乐，有时比朋友自己还先知道朋友需要什么。这是双鱼的星座，两条鱼朝相反的方向游动，一个由海王星守护（传统上为木星）的变动水象星座，它的本性流动、富于想象，而且深怀慈悲。",
 "As the last sign of the zodiac, Pisces is often said to carry a little of every sign before it. That gives Pisces people an unusual capacity to understand others: they can empathise with almost anyone, see the hurt behind bad behaviour and forgive what others cannot. Water makes them emotionally responsive; mutability makes them adaptable, able to shift shape to fit whoever and whatever is in front of them.": "作为黄道带的最后一个星座，双鱼座常被说成带着之前每个星座的一点点。这让双鱼座的人有一种不同寻常的理解他人的能力：他们几乎能与任何人共情，看见恶劣行为背后的伤痛，原谅别人无法原谅的事。水让他们在情感上敏于回应；变动让他们善于适应，能够改变形状去契合眼前的任何人、任何事。",
 "The gifts are rare. Pisces is often creative, intuitive and spiritually curious, drawn to art, music, poetry, dreams, nature and the sea. Its kindness can be extraordinary, and its imagination can turn an ordinary Tuesday into something enchanted. Yet that same openness means Pisces can absorb other people's moods, lose track of its own needs, and drift away from practical tasks when reality feels too harsh.": "这些天赋很罕见。双鱼座常常富有创造力、直觉敏锐，对灵性充满好奇，被艺术、音乐、诗歌、梦境、大自然和大海吸引。它的善良可以非同寻常，它的想象力能把一个平凡的星期二变成某种被施了魔法的东西。然而同样的敞开也意味着双鱼座可能吸收别人的情绪，忘了自己的需要，并在现实显得太过严酷时从实际事务中漂走。",
 "The growth edge for Pisces is boundaries — not to close the door to the mystical, but to know where it ends and others begin. When Pisces learns to say no, to give itself the compassion it offers everyone else, and to anchor its dreams in daily routines, it becomes a powerful healer and maker. The two fish can then swim together: one in the dreaming depths, the other in the shallows of everyday life, both of them free.": "双鱼座的成长课题是边界——不是对神秘之物关上门，而是知道自己在哪里结束、别人从哪里开始。当双鱼座学会说“不”，把它给予所有人的慈悲也给予自己，并把梦想锚定在日常规律中，它就会成为一位强大的疗愈者和创造者。那时两条鱼就可以一起游：一条在梦的深处，另一条在日常生活的浅滩，两条都是自由的。",
 "Pisces people have an enormous capacity for compassion. They listen without judgement, sense what is unspoken and often make others feel deeply understood. Their imagination is rich and original, and many with this Sun have a natural feel for art, music, writing, dance or anything that carries emotion beyond words. They are adaptable and gentle, able to flow with change in ways that would unsettle more rigid signs. Intuition is a genuine strength here; Pisces often knows things through feeling before logic catches up. They are also capable of great selflessness, giving time, care and creativity to people and causes they believe in, and inspiring others to soften, dream and hope.": "双鱼座的人有着巨大的慈悲能力。他们不带评判地倾听，感知未说出口的东西，常常让别人觉得被深深理解。他们的想象力丰富而独创，许多太阳在双鱼的人对艺术、音乐、写作、舞蹈或任何承载着言语之外情感的东西有天然的感觉。他们善于适应而温和，能够以会让更僵硬的星座不安的方式随变化流动。直觉在这里是一种真正的力量；双鱼座常常在逻辑跟上之前就通过感受知道了一些事。他们也能做到极大的无私，把时间、关怀和创造力献给他们相信的人和事业，并激励别人变得柔软、去做梦、去希望。",
 "The Pisces shadow is a tendency to dissolve. Pisces people can take on other people's emotions so completely that they lose sight of their own, and they may find it hard to say no, ending up drained or quietly resentful. Escapism can become a pattern — daydreaming, endless scrolling, avoiding difficult conversations or decisions until circumstances make them instead. They may idealise people and then feel crushed when those people turn out to be human. Practical tasks, deadlines and paperwork can slide. Sometimes Pisces casts itself as the rescuer or the martyr. The constructive work is to build gentle structure into daily life, to protect its energy, and to trust that boundaries make compassion sustainable rather than smaller.": "双鱼座的阴影是一种溶解的倾向。双鱼座的人可能把别人的情绪吸收得太彻底，以至于看不见自己的情绪，他们也可能很难说“不”，最终被掏空或悄悄地心怀怨气。逃避可能成为一种模式——做白日梦、无休止地刷手机、回避艰难的谈话或决定，直到形势替他们做出决定。他们可能把人理想化，然后在那些人原来只是凡人时感到崩溃。实际的事务、截止日期和文书工作可能被搁下。有时双鱼座会把自己塑造成拯救者或殉道者。建设性的功课是为日常生活建立温和的结构，保护自己的能量，并相信边界让慈悲变得可持续，而不是变得更小。",
 "Pisces loves with its whole heart and imagination. Pisces people are romantic in the truest sense: they notice tiny gestures, write the message that brings tears to your eyes, and can make ordinary moments feel touched by magic. They seek a soul-level connection, a partner who understands their feelings, their dreams and their need for quiet.": "双鱼座用整颗心和全部的想象力去爱。双鱼座的人是最真正意义上的浪漫：他们注意到细微的举动，写出让你热泪盈眶的消息，能让平凡的时刻仿佛被魔法触碰过。他们寻求灵魂层面的连接，一个理解他们的感受、梦想和对安静的需要的伴侣。",
 "The risk is losing themselves in a relationship, adapting so much to a partner that their own desires disappear, or seeing someone through a rose-tinted veil and missing the warning signs. Pisces may also avoid conflict by drifting away rather than saying what is wrong. Healthy Pisces love blends devotion with clarity. It thrives with a partner who is kind, emotionally honest and steady enough to offer an anchor without making Pisces feel caged. Speaking needs aloud, even when it feels unromantic, helps the dream become a lasting reality.": "风险在于在一段关系中迷失自己，为伴侣调整得太多以至于自己的愿望消失了，或者透过玫瑰色的面纱看一个人，错过了警示信号。双鱼座也可能通过漂走而不是说出哪里不对来回避冲突。健康的双鱼式爱情把全心付出与清醒融合在一起。它在一个善良、情感诚实、足够稳定、能提供一个锚而又不让双鱼座觉得被关进笼子的伴侣身边茁壮成长。把需要大声说出来，即使那感觉一点也不浪漫，也能帮助梦想变成持久的现实。",
 "Pisces people flourish in work that lets them use their imagination or care for others. Art, music, film, writing, photography, design, counselling, social care, spiritual work, charity and anything near water can all suit them. They often sense what people need before it is spoken, and they bring warmth and creativity to any team they join.": "双鱼座的人在能运用想象力或照顾他人的工作中蓬勃发展。艺术、音乐、电影、写作、摄影、设计、咨询、社会关怀、灵性工作、慈善，以及任何靠近水的事情，都很适合他们。他们常常在别人说出口之前就感知到别人需要什么，并为加入的任何团队带来温暖和创造力。",
 "Highly competitive environments, harsh criticism and rigid bureaucracy can be draining. Pisces may struggle with deadlines, self-promotion or setting a fair price for its work, and it can quietly absorb a team's stress. The professional growth edge is structure: clear schedules, a trusted colleague who enjoys detail, and firm boundaries around availability. When Pisces values its gifts and organises its days around them, it can produce work that moves people deeply.": "高度竞争的环境、严厉的批评和僵化的官僚体系可能让人精疲力竭。双鱼座可能在截止日期、自我推销或为自己的工作定一个公道的价格上遇到困难，也可能悄悄吸收团队的压力。职业上的成长课题是结构：清晰的日程，一位喜欢细节的可信赖的同事，以及在可联系时间上坚定的边界。当双鱼座珍视自己的天赋，并围绕它们安排每一天时，它能创造出深深打动人的作品。",
 "Pisces people need regular time to clear away what they have absorbed from others. Water is naturally restorative for this sign: a bath with a handful of sea salt, a swim, a walk along the shore, or even a few minutes listening to rain. Music, daydreaming and creative play are not indulgences here but essential nourishment. Gentle grounding helps too, such as a simple morning routine or time with your feet in the grass. Keep a dream journal beside the bed, and on the new moon write down one boundary you want to hold with love.": "双鱼座的人需要定期的时间，来清理他们从别人那里吸收的东西。水对这个星座有天然的修复作用：加一把海盐泡个澡，游个泳，沿着海岸散步，甚至只是花几分钟听雨。音乐、做白日梦和创造性的玩耍在这里不是放纵，而是必不可少的滋养。温和的落地练习也有帮助，比如一个简单的晨间规律，或者让双脚踩在草地上待一会儿。在床边放一本梦境日记，并在新月时写下一条你想带着爱去守住的边界。",
 "Pisces often feels deeply understood by the other water signs, Cancer and Scorpio, who share its emotional depth and intuition. Earth signs — Taurus, Virgo and Capricorn — can offer the stability and practical support Pisces sometimes lacks; Virgo, the opposite sign, often feels like a complementary teacher of order and discernment. Fire signs bring excitement and confidence, though Pisces may need gentleness when fire moves too fast. Air signs bring fresh ideas and perspective, yet both may need to work at emotional understanding. As ever, the whole birth chart matters far more than the Sun sign alone.": "双鱼座常常觉得被另外两个水象星座巨蟹座和天蝎座深深理解，它们共享它的情感深度和直觉。土象星座——金牛座、处女座和摩羯座——能提供双鱼座有时缺少的稳定和实际支持；对宫的处女座常常像一位互补的老师，教它秩序与分辨力。火象星座带来兴奋和自信，不过当火走得太快时，双鱼座可能需要温柔对待。风象星座带来新鲜的想法和视角，但双方都可能需要在情感理解上下功夫。一如既往，整张星盘远比单看太阳星座重要。"
}
